+# ARC3_VERIFY: escalation-gated verification tools. Off by default; off, no
+# code path below changes a request, a tool result or an artifact.
+#
+# The harness informs and the model decides every action. Once a level has
+# stalled - ARC3_VERIFY_TOKENS generated on it, or ARC3_VERIFY_ACTIONS actions
+# taken on it without a level-up - two cheap hypothesis tests become callable
+# from the python sandbox for the rest of that level: replay_check(sim_fn)
+# (the model's simulator against the level's recorded transitions, beside a
+# nothing-changes baseline) and action(..., expect=[...]) (per-step stated
+# expectations; the batch halts at the first contradiction). Gated rather than
+# always on because always-on world-modelling measured about +95% actions on
+# easy levels (Retrodict), and offered rather than forced because
+# actor-requested modelling beat auto-repair (Tycho). One opener line says the
+# tools exist; their documentation lives in the sandbox (`verify_docs`), not in
+# every prompt.
+#
+# ARC3_VERIFY_GATE: stall (tokens OR actions, default) | tokens | actions |
+# always (armed from the level's first turn - the always-on control) | off.
